  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Results condition on 36 retained ICML 2026 Spotlight papers (after excluding 14 of 50 for missing code/artifacts, >100 H100h compute or multi-node setups, or closed-API reliance) and 1,029/1,463 (70.3%) compatible tasks; 434 tasks failed reference verification (183 mismatch, 186 blocked, 65 resource/access) and do not represent a conference-wide reproduction rate.",
    "Five human-verified reference observations are a protocol choice rather than a statistical guarantee of complete uncertainty coverage; numerical compatibility does not certify scientific correctness, and RRAs can preserve flawed assumptions or introduce incorrect choices (84 numerical reversals).",
    "Automated post-hoc Auditors remain imperfect against 818 two-person human labels: Codex misses 8/39 (20.5%) and Claude misses 15/39 (38.5%) confirmed violations (with 4/779 = 0.5% false positives each). Separate static Aligner analysis also recorded 238 paper-code contradiction findings across 669 tasks.",
    "Reported -19.7% downstream API savings and 8–13 round API break-even cover downstream Reproducer API usage only, excluding $5,026 build API, Auditor API, 8x H100 GPU runtime, 5-person human verification, and ongoing maintenance.",
    "Ordinary outputs vs. Full RRA compares two separate upstream workflows together rather than isolating file reorganization on identical outputs; component ablations measure losses conditional on remaining components; cross-vendor model comparisons are descriptive due to differing CLI harnesses; and human researcher reuse was not experimentally tested."
  ],
